{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice","id":1004025,"title":"Aspiration advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-16T11:26:24-08:00","id":1004025,"title":"Aspiration advice","content":"So I running into a situation where my players are choosing ridiculously easy aspirations like going to buy something or doing things like gorging themselves. There's no conflict, story or real achievement with these types of things that i would consider worthy of a beat. So what are some guidelines to recognize a worthy aspiration vs some seemingly mundane task? If stuff like this is legit I don't want to cheat my players either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1485-robwolf","name":"RobWolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1485_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:51:49-08:00","id":1004035,"title":"","content":"Promethean had a system where players got xp for discovering things that highlighted what they were or significant insight toward becoming human. Have you explained that aspirations are supposed to be long term goals to work toward throughout several sessions, not benchmarks signifying a descent into monstrosity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-04-2017, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:57:00-08:00","id":1004037,"title":"","content":"First of all point out that Aspirations are things the players want to see happen with their characters; not the characters' own goals. I have to say they're a really dull bunch of players if they honestly want grocery shopping to be an important goal in their character's personal arc no matter how important it actually is for the characters to get supplies.<br /> But for actual guidelines, Aspirations generally fit into three types:<br /> * Aspirations that they know or strongly suspect will trigger a conflict<br /> * Aspirations they don't yet know how to achieve (as in they require research or exploration which gives you ample opportunity to add conflict)<br /> * Aspirations that will negatively affect their characters in a dramatic fashion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:59:41-08:00","id":1004041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1004035#post1004035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pronethean had a system where players got xp for discovering things that highlighted what they were or significant insight toward becoming human. Have you explained that aspirations are supposed to be long term goals to work toward throughout several sessions, not benchmarks signifying a descent into monstrosity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only one of the Aspirations are intended to be long-term. The other two should, if possible, be stuff that could happen within one session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:35:18-08:00","id":1004060,"title":"","content":"Are they doing that to gain beats for cheap ? I mean, aside from trying to game the system, I don't really see why they would pick such mundane stuff for aspirations. Maybe they're new players, and this is their first game so they fuck around with the system a bit ? Yeah, I don't know. If that's the case, then, I imagine they'll grow out of it after two or three sessions, once they realize it doesn't serve any purpose. As long as you provide an engaging story on your side, they should follow once they're done buying groceries.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, try to talk to them and ask them why they are so insistant on doing that. If they're just doing it for the lulz, then, you can ignore that, or, if you're up for it, play their game and make their super boring aspiration an epic goal. They wanna go to the grocery store to buy canned food (that they're not even gonna eat ?), have the Lancea Sanctum and Circle of the Crone show up to have a gang war inside the store. Now, the player has to find a clerk who hasn't fled, force him to check their items and pay them. For extra drama, maybe the credit card machine eats a bullet and the player has to pay with cash, or worse, check. As they take out their coins, a sanctified gangrel directs a swarm of locusts to fill the place, causing the player to drop their money, and one coin rolls under a big shelf that holds flammable goods. What if the clerk dies and the player has to embrace them so they can complete their shopping ? They'll be too freaked out to comply, the player asks to speak to the manager. Turns out the manager is a pack of Werewolves who then join the fight.<br /> <br /> Or if things are really unmanageable, you could just scratch the aspiration system. Basically, all it is is a space on your sheet where you write down the kind of things you tend to talk about with your GM when you want something to happen to your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 11-16-2016, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:35:47-08:00","id":1004061,"title":"","content":"Or advise them to write at least one Aspiration as want of Beast in them if they not have better ideas - yeah, you heard it right. Beast. Let one need to hunt in time of play. Let other to engage in Blood Bonds on him. They are one short scenes, but add drama to vampire life, is it not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T21:04:56-08:00","id":1004233,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't even think of them as long term and short term. <br /> <br /> *I want my character to gain political influence. <br /> <br /> -steps I could take: <br /> 1) befriend other kindred, if a player devotes time to improve his impression rating with other kindred (regardless of success or failure of dice) gain a beat. Most kindred have allies and enemies, befriending this kindred could gain him enemies. <br /> <br /> 2) show up at social events, and voice his opinion (regardless of dice rolls gain a beat). He could gain support or make other kindred angry, adds to the story. <br /> <br /> Aspirations can be meta.<br /> <br /> I want my character to learn this weird esoteric devotion. <br /> <br /> *steps<br /> <br /> 1) Research common devotions whether through social interaction or actual occult studies. <br /> <br /> 2) burn through lots of blood with the discipline in question forcing lots of feeding. Plenty of interesting story fodder here. <br /> <br /> Aspirations don't have to benefit the character. <br /> <br /> My ally wants to be the sheriff and I will help him. <br /> <br /> 1) discredit the current sheriff in social circles. (Helps to have actual dirt but not needed. Gossip is good too) I guarantee interesting story hooks here. <br /> <br /> 2) petition the powers that be on his behalf. (Helps if you have clout or numbers)<br /> <br /> 3) building off 2 convince others to petition on his behalf. <br /> <br /> Many of these steps can be used multiple times. Some are limited by social impression. The rest no more than once per game anyway. <br /> <br /> The important part is most of these can lead to interesting story, ask them what they want to take away from the game; great stories or stories about their character shopping for pet treats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T09:07:16-08:00","id":1004455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice#post1004025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ridiculously easy aspirations like going to buy something or doing things like gorging themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gorging themselves how? If they're going for Blood Beats by shameless overfeeding, remind them that consistently treating their territory like a six-block Big Gulp comes with consequences. Also, if other vampires find out they'll probably catch flack for being overindulgent and/or irresponsible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:31:52-08:00","id":1004548,"title":"","content":"Like most new story-mechanics in 2E, Aspirations are supposed to be <i>dramatic </i>things.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the aspiration itself will be obviously dramatic. &quot;Overthrow the Sheriff who wronged me.&quot; &quot;Blackmail the Harpy&quot; &quot;Learn the secret about my Grandsire that my Sire doesn't want me to know.&quot;<br /> <br /> But sometimes the aspiration won't be obviously dramatic, and that's where you come in. &quot;Spend more time with my Touchstone&quot; - On the surface, what a nice double-dip! Beats and Willpower refreshes for the same scene. And that's where you step in to make things dramatic as the ST. The touchstone can't spend time with the PC until <i>this terrible problem</i> is solved. Or, <i>because I've just fallen in love and am in the honeymoon phase</i>. Now the PC has to make some dramatic choices of their own.<br /> <br /> On some level, it doesn't matter what they put down, because whatever gets put down, you should be thinking of ways to make it dramatic or conflicted.<br /> <br /> No free lunches. And if you need help thinking how to spin something dramatic/interesting that seems boring, we're here to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T04:19:19-08:00","id":1004871,"title":"","content":"I agree with Holy. Aspiration Beats should be acheived *through conflict*. Obviously I don't mean just punching faces. <br /> <br /> &quot;Show up the vampire who embarassed me at Elysium&quot; is conflict.<br /> &quot;Find out why my Sire abandoned me&quot; also is.<br /> &quot;Go shopping for a new fur coat&quot; isn't. Unless it's made from a Werewolf, and owned by a vampire who doesn't want to part with it.<br /> <br /> There ought to be a force of opposition. An adequately powerful force.<br /> <br /> Beating up the leader of the Carthians? Sure. <br /> Beating up a newborn baby? No. Unless the baby is....<br /> <br /> What are the *specific* worst examples of players choices of Aspirations, or attempts at gaining Beats?<br /> <br /> The thing to do is cut the cheap ones off before they ever get started.<br /> &quot;I have an Aspiration to go shopping&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, if you do, you're going to have to explain to me how there's any realistic conflict or opposition there. Because I'm not giving you a point for shoe shopping at Macy's. Not in this lifetime.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, OK then. How about...&quot;<br /> <br /> There is nothing wrong with it being a negotiation with the player. And remember: they're not the final arbiter of what constitutes an Aspiration or Beat. You are. Let them know that, so they know where they are. Then be firm (if needed), but fair.<br /> <br /> I think aspirations are there primarily for two reasons:<br /> - to allow the player to guide you towards what they'd like to do.<br /> - to help you to create scenes of dramatic conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","user":"FutureBondVillain","date":". 11-18-2016, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T09:59:14-08:00","id":1004997,"title":"","content":"I don't really think Aspirations need to be so strict. They basically replace the two freebie XP you got in 1e (attending and learning something or whatever it was).<br /> <br /> Remember that two of the three are meant to be accomplished in a single session. I don't know about you, but I don't have time to give every single player in my group two &quot;conflicts&quot; to be resolved every session, let alone do so while still providing progress with the main plot and providing feeding scenes.<br /> <br /> As long as it engages the players and provides you some hint as to where they want to go with their characters, it's good enough for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:26:12-08:00","id":1005013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice#post1004025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I running into a situation where my players are choosing ridiculously easy aspirations like going to buy something or doing things like gorging themselves. There's no conflict, story or real achievement with these types of things that i would consider worthy of a beat. So what are some guidelines to recognize a worthy aspiration vs some seemingly mundane task? If stuff like this is legit I don't want to cheat my players either.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have veto powers on stupid aspirations like &quot;Drawing in another breath&quot; or &quot;having a piece of candy&quot; (barring narrative situations in which those aspirations have a gravitas and are compelling, like being confined to submarine depths, or without supplies in the middle of a desert). Exercise it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:24:13-08:00","id":1005103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1004997#post1004997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really think Aspirations need to be so strict. They basically replace the two freebie XP you got in 1e (attending and learning something or whatever it was).</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, no they don\u2019t. Beyond the fact the entire metric of XP award and cost has changed utterly, you already get one \u201cfree\u201d beat per session (that has nothing to do with Aspirations). You don\u2019t need to replace it because it\u2019s still there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember that two of the three are meant to be accomplished in a single session. </div> </div> </div>Where does it say this? Because in CoD it says precisely \u201cyou should aim for accomplishing about one Aspiration per session\u201d (p. 28)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know about you, but I don't have time to give every single player in my group two &quot;conflicts&quot; to be resolved every session, let alone do so while still providing progress with the main plot and providing feeding scenes. </div> </div> </div>Well, I can totally understand that. I think group size has a great bearing upon it; the bar would probably have to be raised or lowered depending on that. I have a two PC group, so I can sort of work on a more focused, individual basis. And again, it's \u201cabout one conflict\u201d. Two would be impossible.<br /> Also there\u2019s no reason AFAIC that they can\u2019t, at least at times, have Aspirations that tie in with the main plot in some way or other (tangentially, at least).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As long as it engages the players and provides you some hint as to where they want to go with their characters, it's good enough for me. </div> </div> </div>I think, in narrative discussion, \u201cconflict\u201d is often (incorrectly) assumed to mean something almost always over dramatic. A goal that requires \u201creal (not necessarily excessive) effort\u201d can be said to be achieved under conflict.<br /> \u201cFinding somewhere safe to sleep for the night\u201d works. If the character has to make an effort to do it, say because the neighborhood\u2019s rough, there's environmental factors, or they have to be careful because someone's hunting them.<br /> <br /> But if it\u2019s \u201cI rent a hotel room, and put the \u2019Do Not Disturb\u2019 sign out\u201d\u2026 Yeah I\u2019m not giving you one for that. Unless some problem arises\u2026<br /> <br /> I love Aspirations, but I want them to be meaningful. To provide focus and direction. Not to be used to get a cheap pseudo-XP-point by going shopping every week. That does not help the game at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T15:41:43-08:00","id":1005136,"title":"","content":"I advise looking at the storytelling section. Think it's called will to achieve. I love this twist. It forces the players to want to have interesting aspirations they can delve into.<br /> <br /> This option may not work as well for short games. But if you want a very sandbox long run game I think it is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T18:12:05-08:00","id":1005176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005103#post1005103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where does it say this? Because in CoD it says precisely \u201cyou should aim for accomplishing about one Aspiration per session\u201d (p. 28)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pg. 79<br /> <br /> &quot;Lastly, Aspirations <u><i><b>make for great fodder for quick and easy<br /> goals</b></i></u>. <b>Don\u2019t be afraid to take<i> <u>at least one</u></i> Aspiration without<br /> immense challenge or risk</b>. For example, \u201cFind a safe haven\u201d isn\u2019t<br /> an unreasonable goal, and it gives you something to do during<br /> the first session if you\u2019re struggling to find a place for your<br /> character.<u> <b><i>Look at easy Aspirations as story hooks. In play, try<br /> to involve the other players\u2019 characters in accomplishing them.</i></b></u>&quot;<br /> <br /> Overall pg. 274 also mentions that you don't have to achieve the goals of meaningful Aspirations to get a Beat, and they can even be meta, like 'lash out at a defenseless human&quot; or &quot;learn a new skill/discipline/whatever&quot; or even &quot;use discipline in some cool way&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 I<b>t\u2019s important to remember that grander Aspirations can award<br /> Beats any time the character takes meaningful steps toward<br /> resolution; don\u2019t punish players for taking lofty goals.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 <b>Aspirations can be \u201cmeta.\u201d The player knows them; the<br /> character doesn\u2019t have to</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> An interesting thing from that page is this;<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>As it stands, they\u2019re mostly open-ended \u2014 players can do with them what they please</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> They really are supposed to be constantly providing their Beats and driving the story forward. Of course the ST can and should veto overtly silly stuff if that will subtract from the plot, but overall you should let your players decide on where they want to go with them.<br /> <br /> So be fast and loose with them. As long as the players, including you, are having fun and the Aspirations are driving the story forward, its all good.<br /> <br /> They wanna get supplies, make the store they choose to stop at be someone else's territory they accidentally invade. Gorging themselves is a fine aspiration. Dead bodies are stories. And gluttonous Kindred quickly slide in Humanity and may attract even more evil shit or the victim's families/protectors/friends/lovers/owners/whatevers. Make them inadvertently dry up someone's ghoul. Or if you're into throwing other monsters in, kinfolk, proximi or whatever else. That stupid beefcake was a Mafia prince, and you are the last one seen with him before he died.<br /> <br /> Remind the players that their Aspirations are supposed to be hooks for you all, together, to develop into stories. They are not MK's &quot;Test your Might!&quot;. It doesn't matter if they are difficult. It matters if they are interesting and provide creative fodder for you all to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 11-18-2016, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T18:24:55-08:00","id":1005181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1004997#post1004997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that two of the three are meant to be accomplished in a single session.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005103#post1005103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does it say this?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005176#post1005176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pg. 79<br /> <br /> &quot;Lastly, Aspirations <u><i><b>make for great fodder for quick and easy<br /> goals</b></i></u>. <b>Don\u2019t be afraid to take<i> <u>at least one</u></i> Aspiration without<br /> immense challenge or risk</b>. For example, \u201cFind a safe haven\u201d isn\u2019t<br /> an unreasonable goal, and it gives you something to do during<br /> the first session if you\u2019re struggling to find a place for your<br /> character.<u> <b><i>Look at easy Aspirations as story hooks. In play, try<br /> to involve the other players\u2019 characters in accomplishing them.</i></b></u>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And where in that, or elsewhere, does it say two of the three are meant to be accomplished in the session (which is what I was quoted)?<br /> <br /> I've posted a direct quote (from CoD) that says <b>precisely</b> \u201cyou should aim for accomplishing about one Aspiration per session\u201d (p. 28)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:11:48-08:00","id":1005192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005181#post1005181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And where in that, or elsewhere, does it say two of the three are meant to be accomplished in the session (which is what I was quoted)?<br /> <br /> I've posted a direct quote (from CoD) that says <b>precisely</b> \u201cyou should aim for accomplishing about one Aspiration per session\u201d (p. 28)<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno man, &quot;at least one&quot; implies that maybe you should/could choose more than one to be easy? Don't blame a guy for thinking one should be able to accomplish a couple quick and easy goals in a session. You think that should be hard? Isn't that kinda paradoxical?<br /> <br /> You may be quoting precisely, but are you understanding precisely? &quot;About one&quot; could be two or three, you see? Its open ended on purpose.<br /> <br /> I haven't found Maina's quote's suggestion of 2, but the quote you give does not restrict it to one, either. Read page 79 and 274 of VtR2e, which is what the thread is discussing and take the whole thing into context. <br /> <br /> Aspirations are not necessarily in story difficult things. They can be pretty much anything, including OOC things, that a player chooses as a character's goals/next actions. And they can, and many times should, be quick and easy to achieve. And you can surely get Beats for more than one Aspiration per session. Depending on how busy/lucky and how much screen time a player is allotted, they could be easily getting all 3. And then switch them around every session.<br /> <br /> Finding somewhere to sleep is an Aspiration. It doesn't matter if you accomplish it by riding a customized tints Bentley to the Hamptons or hopping on a bus to Cicero at the crack of dawn. There doesn't need to be conflict, there just needs to be a story.<br /> <br /> So if a player gives you a buy a new fur coat Aspiration, maybe he wants to play a scene on a high end retailer and throw his money around. Maybe get the number of that cute store clerk for later. Or get busy on the special shopper rooms.<br /> <br /> Why does it have to be a werewolf pelt? Is this an action movie simulator or something? Why are only confrontational scenes worthy of Aspirations? That may be how you like things, but that is not part of the rules, or even the guidelines suggest how it should be handled.<br /> <br /> And anything that get the story moving is an opportunity for conflict, anyways, if you want to and make it so. People have to go places or have things brought to them. Anything can happen. Even if the players are trying to &quot;farm xp&quot; make an omelette with those eggs. They'll catch on pretty quick. Be loose with the Beats and they won't feel the need to have &quot;dumb&quot; Aspirations.<br /> <br /> A precise quote;<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 It\u2019s important to remember that grander Aspirations can award<br /> Beats any time the character takes meaningful steps toward<br /> resolution; don\u2019t punish players for taking lofty goals.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here is a another precise quote, again, for you;<br /> <br /> &quot;As it stands, they\u2019re mostly open-ended \u2014 players can do with them what they please.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm just engaging in discussion so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1485-robwolf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1485_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1485\" data-vbnamecard=\"1485\">RobWolf</a> can have a different take on things too. And that take says Aspirations are very flexible, be generous with them and their Beats, talk with your players about the scenes they want to play out and have fun. Even if it's just going to 7Eleven to force down a slurpee only to regurgitate it on the poor clerk and then be depressed about how it sucks to be a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:31:58-08:00","id":1005199,"title":"","content":"The last quotes are fine. Re: lofty goals, I've had players take them. And I've told them, you'll get beats for pieces of the goal. I'm not going to only give one goal out for &quot;becoming Prince&quot; after a year of game time. I'm giving one out any time you take a significant step.<br /> <br /> I'm giving beats out for &quot;learning I can breath again, smoke and f*** again&quot; as part of &quot;learn what I've become&quot;. I have no problem with gicing them out if it feels right, even if there wasn't massive conflict, or difficulty attaining it. I just don't, personally, want that to be the norm.<br /> <br /> I don't know what it is with taking a direct quote and trying to make it sound like something else &quot;about one means about one&quot;. If you want to read that as &quot;2 or 3&quot; fine. If That's not how language works, for me. Maybe one, maybe two, maybe none (very rarely three) is how I read it. Overall it's going to be &quot;about one&quot; (as in average out around that mark). If you want to average out 3 that's your prerogative. But I can hardly be seen to be the one diverging, re: award frequency.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of ways to earn beats. Every frenzy. Every humanity roll. Resolving a Condition. Taking a Dramatic Failure. Lethal damage in the last three boxes. And a free one every session. I really don't need to bend over backwards to make sure they get enough beats.<br /> ----------------------<br /> Anyone, thanks for the discourse. I think we've both made our points, so I'll avoid replying further to defend my position, for the avoidance of us going round in circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T20:18:30-08:00","id":1005210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005181#post1005181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And where in that, or elsewhere, does it say two of the three are meant to be accomplished in the session (which is what I was quoted)?<br /> <br /> I've posted a direct quote (from CoD) that says <b>precisely</b> \u201cyou should aim for accomplishing about one Aspiration per session\u201d (p. 28)<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div> Ideally you should be able to ac-complish at least one of these Aspirations per game session<br /> <br /> It references like this in the God Machine chronicles book on page 151, left column, first paragraph, under the sample aspirations. Referring to the 2 short term aspirations. And advising to take no more than 1 very long term aspiration<br /> <br /> I don't think aspirations should have to be completed to gain a beat though. It's worded a little contradictory depending on where you are looking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","user":"overload","date":". 11-18-2016, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:14:28-08:00","id":1005225,"title":"","content":"So I mean. What's the problem? If the players are having a blast telling stories about vampires going to wal mart for groceries then all power to them. So long as the aspirations lead to scenes and activity, it doesn't matter if they are easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:19:25-08:00","id":1005383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005225#post1005225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I mean. What's the problem? If the players are having a blast telling stories about vampires going to wal mart for groceries then all power to them. So long as the aspirations lead to scenes and activity, it doesn't matter if they are easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really nothing. Aspirations should be important to the character. Something we discussed in my thread of how vampires pass the time was the finite about of active time they have. So if it is important enough to do in the small window of Night time that they have then it could be an aspiration. The weight is on the storyteller to strike home that fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T09:50:16-08:00","id":1005390,"title":"","content":"Aspirations explicitly don't have to be important to the character. They can be meta. They should be important to the player. Aspirations can be something the player wants and the character doesn't know about (meet a ghost, when the character doesn't even know they're real) or the character actively doesn't want (get in trouble due to Frenzy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T10:21:38-08:00","id":1005401,"title":"","content":"Aspiration are though to sell to new players.<br /> <br /> Right now i have issues with my group too with them.<br /> <br /> One player got the system right away and he has political ambition for his character so everytime he takes a step forward that ambition i give him a beat. <br /> <br /> The other two players well.....<br /> <br /> One comes from D&amp;D and some very controling D&amp;D games at that so she is kind of passive gamer with little goals and is just so used to DMs giving her the story and she follow along it that i keep drawing blanks when i try to explain/encourage her to think inspirations.<br /> <br /> The other is a very meta player who doesnt want conflict, he just wanna save point and does his best so that nothing ever bad happens to his character. Fortunately he is well..... an idiot so his decisions are so asinine that provoke conflict by the loads but makes the fact of setting aspiration difficult as he tends to try to pass the &quot;going to wallmart&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> My advices are first make them write aspirations at the end of the game and not the start as this give you time to think how to integrate them to the next session.<br /> <br /> And second maybe try to either write the aspiration for the PC yourself, like think what the PC is trying to accomplish and make them aspirations.<br /> <br /> Or just get rid of the system and give a static 2 beats per session and hand out more when PC do something awesome or RP a good scene.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T13:39:36-08:00","id":1005460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005401#post1005401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspiration are though to sell to new players.<br /> <br /> Right now i have issues with my group too with them.<br /> <br /> One player got the system right away and he has political ambition for his character so everytime he takes a step forward that ambition i give him a beat.<br /> <br /> The other two players well.....<br /> <br /> One comes from D&amp;D and some very controling D&amp;D games at that so she is kind of passive gamer with little goals and is just so used to DMs giving her the story and she follow along it that i keep drawing blanks when i try to explain/encourage her to think inspirations.<br /> <br /> The other is a very meta player who doesnt want conflict, he just wanna save point and does his best so that nothing ever bad happens to his character. Fortunately he is well..... an idiot so his decisions are so asinine that provoke conflict by the loads but makes the fact of setting aspiration difficult as he tends to try to pass the &quot;going to wallmart&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> My advices are first make them write aspirations at the end of the game and not the start as this give you time to think how to integrate them to the next session.<br /> <br /> And second maybe try to either write the aspiration for the PC yourself, like think what the PC is trying to accomplish and make them aspirations.<br /> <br /> Or just get rid of the system and give a static 2 beats per session and hand out more when PC do something awesome or RP a good scene.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> those sound like problems with the player buy in and not with the system. If neither of them want to engage with the game as it's meant to be (and the ST is trying to run) that is proactive stories - then no system will work in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T14:20:41-08:00","id":1005475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005460#post1005460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">those sound like problems with the player buy in and not with the system. If neither of them want to engage with the game as it's meant to be (and the ST is trying to run) that is proactive stories - then no system will work in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said the problem was the mechanic just that is sometimes a hard sell to players not used to be &quot;proactive&quot; in that specific way. However i do think players should set the new aspirations at the end of the session and not at the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T14:22:16-08:00","id":1005476,"title":"","content":"Agree with Gratis. It could be a player buy in issue. <br /> <br /> Another pull from the storyteller section. Is the last bit. Think it's like 12 or 13 questions. If you have some new players maybe it would be best to start character creation with that. <br /> <br /> It's more of a round robin approach to background creation. Allow the players to help create bits of the city with it and you have some automatic buy in to your game. <br /> <br /> Plus with that level of personal investment it's hard to not come up with good aspirations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T18:53:15-08:00","id":1005536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005460#post1005460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">those sound like problems with the player buy in and not with the system. If neither of them want to engage with the game as it's meant to be (and the ST is trying to run) that is proactive stories - then no system will work in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Replacing aspirations with a set number of XP hand out would fix it really. Or just take the choice of Aspiration from the players hands. Is just a tiny part of the system and frankly 1st edition worked perfectly without it so is not a fundamental part of the system per say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005476#post1005476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree with Gratis. It could be a player buy in issue.<br /> <br /> Another pull from the storyteller section. Is the last bit. Think it's like 12 or 13 questions. If you have some new players maybe it would be best to start character creation with that.<br /> <br /> It's more of a round robin approach to background creation. Allow the players to help create bits of the city with it and you have some automatic buy in to your game.<br /> <br /> Plus with that level of personal investment it's hard to not come up with good aspirations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats an awful advice. First, the OP game seems already underway so doing a hard reset seems extreme.<br /> <br /> Second, assuming the players are new why would they know how to create a city? New players havent read the book and normally dont know or know very little about the factions and the splat so them making part of the city when they already get blocked with Aspirations seems ill advice. Though i couldnt found the exact system of the 13 question, so maybe there is something i am missing.<br /> <br /> Or thats assuming also that the DM doesnt have a setting city planned and that the player have any idea of what the city they are playing is like.<br /> <br /> Third, if the players are advantage-minded players like the OP mention then giving them control of the city just gonna make even more advantages on their PCs favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-19-2016, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T19:13:11-08:00","id":1005538,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;13 questions&quot; is a reference to Climbing the Ladder, page 282. It's actually twelve steps, each one answering a question and creating an NPC or a connection to an existing NPC. In my experience, it takes an absurd amount of time and effort. May not be for every group.<br /> <br /> It's not really a system that can be used by the players to their own advantage, though. Most of it is people you've hurt or who have something on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T19:32:26-08:00","id":1005545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005538#post1005538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;13 questions&quot; is a reference to Climbing the Ladder, page 282. It's actually twelve steps, each one answering a question and creating an NPC or a connection to an existing NPC. In my experience, it takes an absurd amount of time and effort. May not be for every group.<br /> <br /> It's not really a system that can be used by the players to their own advantage, though. Most of it is people you've hurt or who have something on you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, i found it. Its....interesting, dont know how it would fix the OP particular problem and i would definetly not use it with people struggling with Aspirations.<br /> <br /> However, i see it could work when the ST doesnt have any set idea for the game and just wanna run &quot;Typical&quot; Requiem with somewhat experience players. Then the player can suggest something that mold the setting into something unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:29:23-08:00","id":1006059,"title":"","content":"Actualy Climbing the Ladder REALLY helped me with one type of player OP seems to suffer from: That's the &quot;i'm intouchable, and I'll avoid any risk/problems for my characters&quot;. As soon as I used that system, a player who would continuously create McNinjas with no family or anything - he made up an entire family with problems and shit, just to milk that XP. Since then he got much better in doing the same with his other characters too, even where we don't use the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T10:54:59-08:00","id":1006770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004025-aspiration-advice?p=1005536#post1005536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Replacing aspirations with a set number of XP hand out would fix it really. Or just take the choice of Aspiration from the players hands. Is just a tiny part of the system and frankly 1st edition worked perfectly without it so is not a fundamental part of the system per say.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thats an awful advice. First, the OP game seems already underway so doing a hard reset seems extreme.<br /> <br /> Second, assuming the players are new why would they know how to create a city? New players havent read the book and normally dont know or know very little about the factions and the splat so them making part of the city when they already get blocked with Aspirations seems ill advice. Though i couldnt found the exact system of the 13 question, so maybe there is something i am missing.<br /> <br /> Or thats assuming also that the DM doesnt have a setting city planned and that the player have any idea of what the city they are playing is like.<br /> <br /> Third, if the players are advantage-minded players like the OP mention then giving them control of the city just gonna make even more advantages on their PCs favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your right it may not work for the existing game. <br /> <br /> Climbing the ladder does most of the work for you in very in depth QnA. If you have ever watched a movie, TV show or read a book you can figure it out. <br /> <br /> Please read climbing the ladder before writing. It's not complete city creation rules. It just helps you pin down important npcs for the player.<br /> <br /> This was more a suggestion for the next game the OP runs. I don't know if it would be a good idea to do this for every game. But if you want a long running sandbox it can help. <br /> <br /> But it's not for everybody. To each their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T13:18:31-08:00","id":1012744,"title":"","content":"I don't know the minds of your players, OP, but I utterly loathe Aspirations. They feel like a bullshit guessing game, because as soon as things actually happen there will be all sorts of ways to go with anything, and I face the choice of following Aspirations or following the interesting stuff that comes up. So I either get screwed out of advancement, or screwed out of following the interesting spontaneous threads. A lot of the time it feels like the only way to 'win' is to pick the cheesiest meta bullshit, which is the opposite of the purpose they're supposed to serve. <br /> Except the text itself advises going with the cheesy meta bullshit.<br /> <br /> So, OP, now that I'm done letting the rant out, I suggest that you check with your players and ask what they feel Aspirations actually add to their game. And if they think they need to pick cheesy bullshit just to keep pace with XP, toss Aspirations out as Beat spigots, give 1 or 2 extra beats per session, and treat Aspirations as just a wish list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 12-13-2016, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}